{
 "format": "Map spec 1.0",
 "id": "europe-borders-through-time-lab",
 "version": "0.1.0",
 "why": "LAB map. Tests the ArcGIS Online time slider (November 2026) on one layer that holds every border change the source records from 1914 to 1947. Not a lesson map and not for MapMaker until ETH Zurich confirms permission.",
 "item": {
  "title": "LAB: Europe's borders through time, 1914 to 1947 v0.1",
  "snippet": "Test map: move the time slider to see Europe's country borders on any date from 1914 to 1947. Draft.",
  "description": "<p><b>Test map.</b> One layer holds every border in Europe that the source records between 1914 and 1947. The time slider shows the borders in force on one date. It steps a year at a time.</p><p><b>Colour:</b> each country keeps one colour for the whole period, so a change of shape or a new country stands out. The colours only tell neighbours apart; they have no other meaning. Every country is also named on the map.</p><p><b>Notes:</b> the source records recognised borders, not wartime occupation, so Poland, Czechoslovakia and Austria stay on the map from 1939 to 1945. Yearly steps skip borders that lasted less than a year. The smallest states are left out, the Soviet Union is one area, coastlines are simplified and the layer stops at 60 degrees east.</p><p><b>Source:</b> CShapes 2.0, ETH Zurich: Schvitz, Girardin, Ruegger, Weidmann, Cederman and Gleditsch (2022), Mapping the International System, 1886-2019, Journal of Conflict Resolution 66(1).</p><p><i>Map version 0.1 (19 November 2026), lab draft.</i></p>",
  "tags": [
   "World History",
   "Europe",
   "borders",
   "time",
   "First World War",
   "Second World War",
   "lab",
   "draft",
   "licence pending"
  ],
  "credits": "CShapes 2.0: Schvitz, Girardin, Ruegger, Weidmann, Cederman and Gleditsch (2022), ETH Zurich; Esri.",
  "license": "Boundaries from CShapes 2.0 (ETH Zurich), licence CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Written permission to use it in MapMaker has not been confirmed: keep this map private until it is. Text written for this map is original."
 },
